This code implements a robust backend system for analyzing source code changes using Git commands. Its primary function is to automate the process of calculating file differences (diffs) across various states—including comparing between designated branches and identifying local modifications in the working directory.

The structure allows comprehensive tracking of repository state, providing granular insights into what files have been committed, modified, or recently added. By executing commands like `git diff` and `git status`, the system establishes a reliable baseline for change detection during CI/CD pipelines or code analysis features.

Handling local changes is critical for development workflows, ensuring that uncommitted work in the current branch (relative to a target branch) is accurately captured. Furthermore, using `shortstat` allows quick programmatic assessment of the scope of changes before deeper diff retrieval.

Overall, this module provides essential data foundation for build tools and automated code reviewers by offering accurate change visibility across the entire software development lifecycle.
